.el .ds Aq '
.TH ag-remote-add 1  "add 0.2.0-rc.3" 
.SH NAME
ag\-remote\-add \- Add a remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag remote add\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-env\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-\-ca\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fINAME\fR> <\fIURL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a remote
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR
Remote to use (default: origin)
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-env\fR \fI<TOKEN_ENV>\fR
Environment variable holding the credential
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-stdin\fR
Read the credential from stdin and store it in `.ag/credentials/<name>` (mode 0600)
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-file\fR \fI<CA_FILE>\fR
Extra CA certificate (PEM) to trust
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Name, e.g. origin
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>
`http(s)://host:port/owner/name`
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0\-rc.3
